                "event": "Rip Current Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued October 12 at 1:30PM CDT until October 12 at 7:00PM CDT by NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...Gulf-facing beaches, including the Matagorda\nPeninsula, Brazoria County beaches, Galveston Island and the\nBolivar Peninsula.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 PM CDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Rip currents can sweep even the best swimmers away\nfrom shore into deeper water.",
                "instruction": "Swim near a lifeguard and away from rocks, jetties, and piers. If\ncaught in a rip current, relax and float. Don't swim against the\ncurrent. If able, swim in a direction following the shoreline. If\nunable to escape, face the shore and call or wave for help.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
