                "event": "Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 12 at 10:35AM CDT by NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nLouisiana...\n\nCalcasieu River near White Oak Park affecting Calcasieu Parish.\n\nCalcasieu River Near Salt Water Barrier affecting Calcasieu Parish.\n\n...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNeches River at Neches River Saltwater Barrier affecting Orange,\nHardin, Jasper and Jefferson Counties.\n\nFor the Calcasieu River...including Glenmora, Oakdale, Oberlin,\nKinder, White Oak Park, Salt Water Barrier...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\nFor the Neches River...including Town Bluff, Evadale, Neches River\nSaltwater Barrier...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Neches River at Neches River Saltwater Barrier.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 5.0 feet, Water is about two feet over portions of\nFour Oaks Ranch Road.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:15 AM CDT Monday the stage was 3.8 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage late\nthis afternoon and continue rising to 4.1 feet this evening.\nAdditional rises are possible thereafter.\n- Flood stage is 4.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
